WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
The Start of Troubles Ahead

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.070
When was that thing built?

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.240
Report it to headquarters imme—

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.660
A hundred out of a hundred. Not bad at all.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.150
Looks like they found us, Cain.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.200
All according to plan.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.410
One Week Later

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.500
The fortress was found here, in Bold Creek.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.940
If they cross through the Central Mountains,

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.350
there's nothing to stop them 
from getting to the capital.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:39.110
They basically have a knife at our throats.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.210
What shall we do, Mr. President?

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:46.440
Hit the fortress with everything 
we have and make it fall.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.480
I-It's going to be a war... 
It's happening again.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.230
Tell me everything you know,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.410
former leader of the Incarnate squad, 
Hank Henriette.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:18.110
Tell me the abilities, weaknesses, 
and hiding locations

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.680
of all of the remaining Incarnates. 
Do not conceal anything from me.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.410
It was a mistake to rely on Incarnates.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.970
We must eliminate every last one.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.910
Claude Withers...

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.040
You must be Cain's younger brother.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.710
Yes, that's right.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:41.340
And as his younger brother,
I will take him down.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.560
No matter what it takes.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.470
Tell me!

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.500
Why... Why did my brother betray us?!

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.570
What in the world is my brother thinking?!

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.080
What happened?!

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.280
Tell me! Tell me, now!

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.030
There's nothing I can tell you.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.170
The only thing I know is how to end this.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.930
Very well. I'll just have to beat
 the answer out of you!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.100
Please, wait!

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.650
You're both trying to stop the Incarnates.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:19.770
If you share the same goal, 
isn't it possible to work together?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.530
Work together? Ridiculous.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.520
That would only bring act two 
of what happened at Whitechurch.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:32.500
If that happens, I will stop Hank,
 even if it costs me my life.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.220
Major Claude.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.870
We've just received an order.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.540
This is an order directly 
from the president.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.780
What does it say?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.260
We are to head to Bold Creek immediately

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.450
and assist in the mission to take 
over New Patria's fortress.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.470
It was also confirmed that 
Cain Madhouse was seen at this fortress.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.500
You made a wise decision.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.090
There's someone I have to 
deal with first. That's all.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:27.470
It's sort of weird not seeing you 
in your white coat, Hank.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.070
This was one of the conditions 
I had to accept to come along.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.090
This is going to be a joint 
mission with other squads.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.560
We have to make sure the others 
don't find out that he's an Incarnate.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.320
I can get a uniform for you, too, 
if you'd like to wear one.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:41.980
Huh?

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.600
How do I look?

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:49.180
N-No, I think I'll pass...

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.010
That must be the main squad handling 
the capture of the fortress,

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.460
and over there is the fortress, our target.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.450
Welcome to the front lines 
of the Northern army.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.950
I am Colonel Martin Wall, and I will be 
leading this mission to capture the fortress.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:39.370
I'm the leader of the Incarnate elimination squad, 
Coup de Grâce, Major Claude Wi—

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.950
Yes, yes. I'm very much aware.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:46.210
You are the son of our president, after all.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:49.410
I'm sure you've seen our forces.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.570
We already went through quite a bit 
before we even reached the fortress.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:58.710
Our recon unit, and even our smaller scout 
teams, are unable to get near the fortress.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.800
The moment we get too close, 
our men are sniped and killed from afar.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.930
To add insult to injury, the enemy is using 
something as archaic as a bow and arrow.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.020
So you're dealing with the 
Incarnate Centaurus.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.840
An extremely quick, skilled sniper,

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.290
and a professional at defending his base 
and throwing enemy forces into chaos.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:19.030
If you attack in small numbers, he'll take 
you all down with his bow and arrows.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.580
Ah, I'd expect nothing less from 
the Incarnate extermination squad.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.180
You are knowledgeable on the matter.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:28.050
What would be our best bet moving forward?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.670
There's only one thing we can do.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.270
Damn it. I can't see anything.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.930
Why are we doing this at night?

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.330
A night raid?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.100
It will serve as bait to draw him out.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.280
Miles will definitely show himself,

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.520
in order to spread fear 
through his attacking enemies.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.060
Fear?

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:04.460
<i>You may be a skilled archer, 
but even you will miss during the night.</i>

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.640
<i>That's why you will choose</i>

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.280
<i>to fight up close.</i>

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.920
The best way to break down a group 
of foot soldiers is through fear.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.860
He'll use his voice to intimidate the enemy,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.110
shattering their souls with their own screams.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:35.230
That is the strategy he excels at.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.490
Hear my hoof beats and quiver in fear!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.450
I will show you undying fear!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.610
I am Death! Your undeniable end!

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.640
Run!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.720
Running a surprise attack all on your own...

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.020
Instilling fear in your enemies...

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.270
I see some things haven't changed, Miles.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:05.330
You're absolutely correct.
 I haven't changed at all, Captain.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.830
I'll kill any enemy that stands in my way.
 Just like in the previous war.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.500
You're the one who's changed.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.050
We thought we'd be regarded as heroes,

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.490
but instead, we were called Beasts 
and treated as a burden.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.240
Seriously, though. Who's the sane one here?

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.510
So that's why you went along with Cain?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:34.390
Cain took what needed to be taken back...
 A country for us to protect!

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.700
You're running away? How boring!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.090
Fire!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:01.810
I see you're as overconfident as ever.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.490
Your boldness makes you excel 
at charging into the enemy,

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.830
but you lack caution.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.330
That's your weakness.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.490
Well, you can't blame me for being confident.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:20.580
I've grown stronger and stronger 
ever since the war.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.470
You could pretty much call 
me immortal at this point.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.200
I hope this next war will be fun, 
too. Don't you agree, Captain?

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.320
We're grateful for your safe return!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.300
The captain was here, just like you said.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.990
Let us move our pieces to the next position.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.880
Centaurus hasn't appeared 
since the battle last night.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.480
Thanks to that, we were able to set up 
our artillery and create these trenches,

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.890
even though they are rather simple.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:16.060
We will attack the fortress as soon 
as preparations are complete.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.000
Yes, sir.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.360
By the way...

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:24.940
I heard that there was another Incarnate 
spotted during the battle with Centaurus...

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.310
But I'm sure my men were just 
seeing things in their fear.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.510
Besides...

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:35.930
We will make that fortress fall, 
no matter the casualties.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.630
We will do whatever it takes.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.250
That is the mission we are tasked with.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.930
Colonel Martin Wall...

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.850
I heard that he's a hero from the civil war,
 but he is quite a challenge to understand.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.380
He's risking his life to fulfill his duty.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.450
We should follow his example.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:01.560
Yes... I will fulfill my duty.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.250
Cain Madhouse...

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.390
I will take him down with my own hands.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.260
U-Um, can I help you with that?

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:19.450
Absolutely not.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.470
This is dangerous. Don't touch it.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.080
<i>What now? There's nothing I can do!</i>

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.600
<i>I'm just being completely useless!</i>

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:34.140
Goodness, that sigh! Can you 
sound any more depressing?

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.280
Th-That's a lot of stuff...

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.880
I was told to help because 
they're low on people.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.570
Damn that army surgeon...

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.860
Who makes a fragile woman do all this?

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.400
<i>You look pretty strong to me...</i>

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.120
Hey. If you're free, why don't you help me out?

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:51.660
I'd love to!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.970
Are these all medical supplies?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.610
We can never have enough.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.710
This isn't just another Incarnate 
extermination mission.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.710
They have a lot of human 
soldiers on their side, too.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.360
This battle is going to be unprecedented.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:14.460
<i>Incarnates and humans are banding 
together to protect their country?</i>

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:20.350
<i>What is he actually planning?</i>

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.000
There. I've closed up your wound.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.080
Now just rest for a while.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:34.960
Thank you very much!

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.920
Oh, you were watching?

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.700
Though it's my old profession,

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.050
I think I still have the chops to be a doctor.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:53.410
To think a once-renowned doctor is now killing 
thousands of soldiers on the battlefield...

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.740
How ironic.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.260
What's the difference?

00:13:57.260 --> 00:14:00.400
I get thanked whether 
I save them or kill them.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:03.110
Why not go with the quicker option?

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:15.210
We brought this from HQ.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:28.700
Now the preparations are complete.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:31.890
We will begin our plan to capture 
the fortress in the morning.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:54.950
Hank.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.260
Having trouble sleeping?

00:14:58.260 --> 00:14:59.150
Yes...

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.080
Me, too.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:07.580
This feels rather strange.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.900
When we first met, 
you were so unapproachable

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:13.800
that I could never imagine 
you smiling like this.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.720
Well, you <i>did</i> shoot me with 
a rifle the moment we met.

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:21.200
W-Well, what was I supposed to do?

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:23.710
I mean... back then, I...

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.010
Please don't laugh!

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.700
I never knew you were so mean.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:38.040
And I never knew you could be so sulky.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:43.280
I've been focused on fulfilling 
my oath this whole time.

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:46.670
It's the only thing that's 
kept me moving forward.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:51.660
And that won't change.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.980
As long as you're alive,
 you have to keep moving forward.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:56.840
Schaal...

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:00.400
Please come back alive tomorrow.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.240
No matter what.

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:04.890
I will.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:39.630
It's time.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.680
Charge!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:00.320
Follow his lead! To the front lines!

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:09.520
Here they come. Fire!

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:25.960
Yes, those as well. Keep loading them in!

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:00.720
<i>Miles... Where are you?</i>

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.030
I think it's about time.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:08.770
Want to come along?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.630
I have my own matters to attend to.

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:14.270
Is that so? Well, see ya.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:26.740
Did you think you'd be 
safe if you were hiding?

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:35.000
Run! Run!

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.170
Scream even more for me!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.260
We're going to stop him!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.080
Scream!

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.530
Let me hear you scream even more!

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.640
Heya, Captain.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.140
How'd you like my orchestra of screams?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.100
Did it resonate in your heart?

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:38.440
It appears that Miles Byron, 
the doctor, died a long time ago.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:41.250
I'd say it's the opposite.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:45.860
The doctor in me was saved 
once I became an Incarnate.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:52.890
I was on the battlefield as an army surgeon
 long before becoming an Incarnate.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:57.620
Thank you, Doctor.

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:00.600
Now I can return to the front lines.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:18.790
<i>No matter how hard I try, 
lives continue to be lost.</i>

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:25.090
<i>Is there any point to everything 
I'm doing if I can't save anyone?</i>

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.960
We're alive because of you!

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:56.240
Thank you!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.660
<i>I see... So this is right.</i>

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:05.960
If I kill one man on the battlefield, 
I can save the life of a comrade!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:11.540
Screams of despair and words 
of gratitude go together!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:16.620
Now, scream even more for me!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.450
Scream! Scream!

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.920
Scream even more!

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:25.310
Your soul has actually been broken 
for quite some time now, I see.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.620
Bring out our secret weapon on my signal.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:51.460
We will be the victors here.

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:27.170
This time, I'll kill you for good!

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:30.040
We should've perished along with that war!

00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:30.990
Hank!

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:32.170
What... is this?

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:34.130
Do you think Master Cain will be pleased?

00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:35.460
You can't stop me!

00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:39.320
The new world you tried to kill has arrived.

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Those Who Seek
